  "body": "Fixes a missed fixture hit under a spindle-C turn (#486). Two causes, both reproduced on main first.\n\n## What was wrong\n1. **Fixed steel was judged in the part frame only.** For a C move the live tool never leaves its station (+X), so steel there is hit at every C. The part-frame reading only saw it near C 0; `posed_steel::upright_turn` answers Unjudged for that pose, so the part-frame verdict stood. End to end: a Rotary Contour on the mill-turn C bar with a fixed steady at the station had no hit on the far side of the bar (C≈180), and the post gate was silent too.\n2. **Steel riding the part was judged at the wrong pose.** `cl::stamp_c` gave every piece of a split move the move's end axis, while mid-turn the tool points along the diagonal. A chuck jaw on the diagonal at holder radius was silent.\n\n## What changed\n- `crates/cl/src/cl/rotary.rs`: `split` stamps each piece with the station pose at its own C (the move's axis turned by the turn left in the move). The last piece keeps the move's axis bit for bit. The post writes only C for C moves, so the stream and the `c_axis_helix.nc` golden are unchanged.\n- New `crates/sim/src/verify/c_steel.rs`:\n  - `station_poses` reads each C move's pose from its C, so toolpaths cached before this fix are judged right at the gate without regenerating.\n  - `fixed_hits` judges fixed steel in the machine frame along the station ray.\n  - The spindle line is recovered from the stamped tips, then from the op's rotary axis, and used only if every tip sits on its ray within 1e-4 mm. With no line, or an arc or non-finite C move, a C move against fixed steel is a hit (fails closed).\n- `crates/sim/src/verify/workholding.rs`: both `_held` wrappers judge the station-posed path, then add the machine-frame fixed-steel hits. Add-only: no existing verdict loosens.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/486-stamp-c-axis.md`.\n\n## How tested\n- sim `c_axis_fixture` (8). Fail on main: `the_machine_meets_fixed_steel_at_the_station_mid_turn` (line given and line unknown), `a_rapid_turn_past_fixed_steel_convicts_as_a_rapid`, `steel_riding_the_part_meets_the_pose_the_turn_passes_through`, `every_stamped_piece_states_the_station_pose_at_its_own_c`. Also `a_path_stamped_before_486_is_read_at_the_pose_its_c_states`, plus clear and fail-closed controls.\n- app `c_axis_fixture` (2): `fixed_steel_at_the_station_convicts_cuts_on_the_far_side_of_the_bar` (fails on main; checks generation and `posting::fixture_findings`) and an off-station control.\n- Unit tests in `cl::rotary` and `verify::c_steel`.\n- Quick gate (escalated to batch because `cl` changed): every suite green except the known headless-GPU ui tests (no adapter on this Mac). After merging main (#491's `arc_bulge`, a `mod` line conflict): sim `c_axis_fixture`, `posed_fixture`, `fixture_stack_span`, app `c_axis_fixture`, `fixtures` and `c_axis_live` pass; clippy `-D warnings` is clean on cl, sim and app.\n- Verdicts in existing suites are unchanged; the only new verdicts are the newly caught hits.\n\n## Not exercised\nNo posted G-code changes (C-only output and goldens unchanged), so no machine run is needed. May touch the same `verify/mod.rs` area as #488 (a `mod` line at most).\n\nChangelog: Fixture checks under a spindle-C turn judge the tool at its machine station pose: fixed steel at the live-tool station and part-riding steel mid-turn are now caught instead of passing the post gate (#486)\n\nFixes #486\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
